{
  "id": "parts-lab",
  "name": "Parts lab",
  "summary": "A core switch with a four-port card in slot 1, optics in three of its cages, two closets hanging off it, and a spares cupboard.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "claim": "Optics (transceivers) are hot-removable and hot-insertable field-replaceable units: they come out and go in without powering the device off.",
      "cite": "Juniper Networks, Maintain Transceivers, EX4400 Switch Hardware Guide (the page shows no date)",
      "url": "https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/hardware/ex4400/Other/maintaining-transceivers.html",
      "read_on": "2026-10-26"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A modular device reports each card in its slot (FPC, PIC) and each optic under the card it sits in (Xcvr), each with its own part number and serial.",
      "cite": "Juniper Networks, show chassis hardware, Junos CLI reference, MX960 sample output",
      "url": "https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/cli-reference/Other/show-chassis-hardware.html",
      "read_on": "2026-10-26"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Every address in this sample is private address space (10.0.0.0/8).",
      "cite": "RFC 1918, Address Allocation for Private Internets, section 3, Private Address Space",
      "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1918.html",
      "read_on": "2026-10-10"
    }
  ],
